WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.570
You're standing at
this abandoned mine.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.972
You can only see maybe
two or three meters

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.707
in before it's entirely black.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:12.412
But in the kind of haze, you can
see the kind of decrepit, old bits

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:17.417
of previous mining industry
and overwhelmingly,

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:21.020
the squawk all these bats.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.923
Their wings beating
in the darkness.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.459
Oh, you can hear them.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:29.896
And you know what kind
of species are inside?

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.564
And so what
we're doing here is

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.066
basically just checking
to see if there's

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.667
any signs of hunting.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.869
Yes.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.837
So you guys are stopping
people from coming here.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:38.638
That's your job.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.040
Masks on?

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:41.875
Yes.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:45.044
MAN 1: Masks on.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.780
[inaudible] All right.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.715
Let's check it out.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.516
Yeah.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.095
See, you can see
them right here.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.129
[bleep]

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:06.666
Wow.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.234
Wow.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.903
So there's an entire
colony in here.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:10.703
Yeah.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.808
MAN (VOICEOVER): This is
the first time in my life

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:19.512
I've been in a bat cave with
bats flying around my head.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.548
But also, in the
knowledge that bats

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.317
contain viruses that
are dangerous to humans,

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.785
especially in
places like Liberia,

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:28.922
where we know Ebola came
from, where all kinds of other

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.090
viruses that we
don't yet know about.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:34.127
So it really was kind
of quite unnerving.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:34.961
MAN: Wow.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.963
CHRIS: Wow.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.566
MAN (VOICEOVER): It was a
relief to have Chris nearby.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.635
He was quite relaxed
about the whole thing.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.405
CHRIS (VOICEOVER): For me,
because I'm a complete wildlife

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.674
geek, I think that this is one
of the most beautiful things

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.742
that I've seen, even
though I know that there

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.578
is this potential risk.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.980
And people want these
bats right, Chris?

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.281
These are valuable.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.317
In many places, these
are a preferred food

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.885
item, where people
will pay almost

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.020
a premium price for something.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.856
So this would be a
prime hunting ground

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.191
for someone to come in here
and just collect a whole bunch.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.495
OK, so if you came in here
as your average poacher,

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.664
you're not wearing a mask, and
there's no real protection,

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.433
you could easily
pick up any kind of--

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.735
This is the exact type
of almost transmission

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:18.705
scenario, where you are
getting aerosolized urine,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.707
aerosolized feces.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.342
But also, if you're
killing the bats,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.077
you're then exposed directly
to their blood as well.

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.045
Wow.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.046
CHRIS: Yes.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.415
Let's walk in a little bit.

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.817
Wow, it just keeps going.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:36.389
This is absolutely insane.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.925
A lot of the old, iron
ore processing equipment,

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:39.759
I'm guessing.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.027
Is that right?

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.061
And you guys, what
are you looking for?

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:42.896
What have you found?

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:43.830
Moses, what is that?

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:57.810
CHRIS: So a poacher came
in here and set that up.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.379
Yes, exactly.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.880
Yes.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.015
MAN (VOICEOVER):
Moses and his team

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:05.385
find this trap, which
seems to suggest

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.754
that humans have been inside.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.923
CHRIS (VOICEOVER): So you
have hunters, who were staying

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:15.094
in this cave night after night,
being exposed to bat feces,

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:18.031
bat urine, bat bites.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.668
There's actually a horseshoe
bats and a type of fruit bat.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:25.705
Horseshoe bats are known
to be related, potentially,

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:29.042
to COVID and also to Ebola.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:29.876
Oh, wow.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.377
Oh, my God.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.112
CHRIS (VOICEOVER): And we
go further and further back

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:35.048
into the depths of the cave.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.215
And Moses looks down.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.952
And he actually
sees a whole host

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.320
of dead bats on the ground.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.024
CHRIS: Wow.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:45.825
This is insane.

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:53.099
MAN: This is a baby.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.134
CHRIS: Yeah.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.569
Oh, my God.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:04:00.306
This one is probably a
juvenile or sub-adult. This

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.241
one's definitely a juvenile.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:06.145
So what caused this one to die?

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.747
So you almost
wonder if there was

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:11.317
some sort of disease that spread
through this community of bats.

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.819
It would certainly
explain why do

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.487
you have a variety
of different age

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:18.424
classes of bats that are all
dead in the exact same spot.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.026
It feels like this
is something that's

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:23.630
really important to understand.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:26.065
MAN (VOICEOVER): And Chris
is fascinated by this.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.834
And it could be
that these bats have

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.603
died of some kind of virus.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.739
It really does feel like
we're in a front line

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.607
of something unknown.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.943
Young bats should not
be dying basically.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.345
Not like this.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:40.813
And I think,
obviously, the issue is

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.183
if there's a poacher in
here, and there's a dead bat,

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.186
and there's blood or whatever,
so there's a problem.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:48.721
So there's probably
some sort of disease.

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.023
Exactly.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:51.290
CHRIS (VOICEOVER):
Bats were known

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.127
to be the reservoir of Ebola.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.429
It also transmitted to
other types of animals

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.666
and then was
transmitted to humans.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:05.471
This is the exact way that a
new deadly virus could start.

